# Zelly's Nexus Additional Terms (Plus)

The PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 above governs this software.
The following terms are additional conditions specific to Zelly's
Nexus, layered on top of the license above. Where a term below is
more restrictive than the license above, the more restrictive term
applies.

## Study and Contribution

Anyone may view, study, test, and run the source code for any
permitted purpose under the license above. Contributions are
accepted through pull requests as described in CONTRIBUTING.md.

## No Commercial Use

The software and any modified version may not be sold, offered as a
paid service, bundled into a closed-source paid product, or
monetized through advertising or any other form of monetary
compensation, whether direct or passive.

## No Closed Derivatives

Any distribution of the software or a modified version must include
the complete corresponding source code, this file, and a clear
description of the modifications. A closed-source product built on
this software is not permitted.

## Independent Projects Stay Out of Scope

An independent project based on the software is permitted only when
its primary functionality is outside the intended scope of Zelly's
Nexus. A change that fits within the project's scope and could
reasonably be merged must be submitted to this repository through an
issue or pull request instead of being maintained as a separate
project.

Being outside the project's scope does not lift any other term of
this license or its additional terms. An independent project still
follows every rule above: noncommercial use only, complete
corresponding source code on distribution, preservation of this
file and its notices, and the fork and linkage rules below. Being
out of scope only affects whether the project may exist separately
instead of being merged; it does not authorize closed distribution,
commercial use, or any other exception.

Before starting a fork or an independent project, an issue must be
opened first to clarify the intended changes. That issue is where it
gets decided whether the work proceeds as a fork, as a pull request
against this repository, or by hand directly against this repository
if the idea has no code yet.

These terms are kept this strict because having several forks of the
same project scattered across different places, each drifting from
the others, is considered an unnecessary and unwanted outcome for
this project.

## Forks Must Stay Linked

Every fork or redistributed repository containing the software must
remain clearly linked to the original Zelly's Nexus repository,
preserve attribution, preserve this file, and state its relationship
to the original project. A fork that is not linked to the original
repository is unauthorized under these additional terms. The
responsible person or organization must remove it immediately after
notice. These terms cannot force deletion from a hosting service
that the responsible party does not control.

## Attribution Preserved

Copyright notices, attribution notices, project references, and
trademarks must not be removed except where necessary to make
accurate statements about the modified project.
